=== /Users/trang.doan/.claude/skills/dg-obsidian-cdp-verify/SKILL.md ===
     1	---
     2	name: dg-obsidian-cdp-verify
     3	description: Prove an apps/obsidian change works in the real Obsidian app by driving it over the Chrome DevTools Protocol. One command launches or attaches to Obsidian on a test vault slot, builds this worktree into it, runs scenario modules, and writes a scenario matrix plus screenshots for pr-evidence and create-pr. Use for live Obsidian verification before a PR, or when asked "does this actually work in Obsidian?".
     4	---
     5	
     6	# Obsidian CDP verify
     7	
     8	## The one command
     9	
    10	From the worktree root:
    11	
    12	```sh
    13	node ~/.claude/skills/dg-obsidian-cdp-verify/scripts/run.mjs \
    14	  --marker "<string only this change's bundle contains>" \
    15	  --scenario path/to/scenarios.mjs [--scenario more.mjs] [--port 9222] [--skip-build]
    16	```
    17	
    18	It runs claim → doctor → launch → deliver → scenarios → cleanup and prints the `last-run.json` path, the scenario matrix, and the `pr-evidence` args. Exit codes: 0 all pass, 1 failure, 2 no vault available or vault locked, 3 marker missing.
    19	
    20	On exit 2 with `candidates`, follow the `obsidian-vault` skill: ask Trang which vault to take, then run `vault.mjs claim --take` and rerun.
    21	
    22	Write scenario files in the session scratchpad, not the repo.
    23	
    24	## Launch
    25	
    26	- With no `--slot`, the vault is this worktree's `obsidian-vault` lease. `run.mjs` claims a free one if the worktree has no lease yet. This keeps the CDP run in the vault the worktree's watcher builds into.
    27	- `--slot N` is a legacy override. It's a 1-based index into `OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_VAULTS` in `<worktree>/apps/obsidian/.env` and bypasses leases, so use it only when Trang names a slot.
    28	- If Obsidian is running on the debug port, the script attaches.
    29	- If it's running without the port, the script quits Obsidian and relaunches it with `--remote-debugging-port`. Trang approved this; the windows come back.
    30	- If it isn't running, the script launches it with the port.
    31	- It then opens the slot vault through `obsidian://open?path=` and waits for a page target where `.workspace` exists and `app.vault.adapter.basePath` matches the vault.
    32	- It writes the lock `<vault>/.obsidian/dg-verify.lock` (`{pid, branch, startedAt}`) and releases it in `finally`.
    33	
    34	## Doctor
    35	
    36	`scripts/doctor.mjs [--slot N]` is read-only and prints JSON: the resolved vault, the lock and the Obsidian state. It exits 2 if the worktree has no lease, or if another live run holds the lock. A lock left by a dead pid is ignored.
    37	
    38	## Deliver
    39	
    40	`scripts/deliver.mjs --marker <str>` also runs on its own.
    41	
    42	1. `OBSIDIAN_PLUGIN_PATH=<slot plugin dir> tsx scripts/build.ts` runs once in `apps/obsidian`. It also writes `apps/obsidian/dist`, which is gitignored.
    43	2. It greps the vault's `main.js` for `--marker` and fails if the marker is absent.
    44	3. It reloads the plugin. The plugin id and folder are resolved from the manifests.
    45	4. It greps again.
    46	5. It warns about other worktrees' apps/obsidian `dev.ts` watchers that mirror into this vault. Your own worktree's watcher builds the same code, so it isn't flagged.
    47	
    48	The harness also hashes `main.js` before and after the scenarios. If it changed, the run is marked invalid.
    49	
    50	## Drive: scenario contract
    51	
    52	A module's `export default` is one scenario or an array of them:
    53	
    54	```js
    55	export default {
    56	  name: "Search modal renders",                 // matrix row + screenshot name
    57	  input: "run open-node-search",                // matrix text
    58	  expected: "modal with a textbox and footer",  // matrix text
    59	  setup: async (ctx) => ({ /* state; snapshot anything you change */ }),  // optional
    60	  run: async ({ client, json, vault }, state) => {
    61	    await client.evaluate(`return app.commands.executeCommandById(${json(`${vault.pluginId}:open-node-search`)});`);
    62	    await client.waitFor(`!!document.querySelector(".dg-node-search-modal [role=textbox]")`);
    63	    return client.evaluate(`document.querySelectorAll(".dg-search-footer-action").length`);
    64	  },
    65	  expect: (actual, state) => ({ pass: actual > 0, actual: `${actual} footer actions` }),  // or a boolean
    66	  teardown: async (ctx, state) => {},           // optional: restore what setup changed
    67	};
    68	```
    69	
    70	- `ctx` has `client`, `vault` (`root`, `pluginId`, `pluginDir`), `branch`, `json`, `verifyPath(name)` and `writeNote(name, body)`. `writeNote` creates or overwrites `_verify/<branch>/<name>` and returns its path.
    71	- `client` has `evaluate`, `waitFor`, `key`, `typeText`, `pressEscape`, `screenshot`, `reloadPlugin`, `clearModals` and `send` (raw CDP).
    72	- The harness does these for you:
    73	  - Before each scenario, it clears modals and restores the layout captured at the start of the run.
    74	  - After `run`, it takes a screenshot.
    75	  - A thrown error becomes a failing row.
    76	- The worked example is `examples/insert-link-at-cursor.mjs` (ENG-2114, 3 scenarios).
    77	
    78	## Evidence
    79	
    80	- The artifacts go to `<worktree>/local/obsidian-cdp/artifacts/<branch>/<runStamp>/`: `<n>-<slug>.png` and `last-run.json` (`results[]` of `{scenario, input, expected, actual, pass, screenshot}`).
    81	- Paste the printed matrix into create-pr's Evidence section.
    82	- Upload the screenshots with pr-evidence, using the printed args:
    83	
    84	```sh
    85	./apps/roam/node_modules/.bin/tsx ~/.claude/skills/pr-evidence/upload.ts --harness obsidian-cdp <printed args>
    86	```
    87	
    88	## Cleanup
    89	
    90	- Cleanup dismisses modals (Escape, then force-removes leftover `.modal-container`), restores the baseline layout and releases the lock.
    91	- **It never deletes folders or notes.** `_verify/<branch>/` persists, and reruns overwrite its notes.
    92	- Scenarios that change vault or app settings must restore them in `teardown`.
    93	
    94	## Gotchas
    95	
    96	These are the ones the code can't handle for you.
    97	
    98	| Symptom | Cause / fix |
    99	| --- | --- |
   100	| Double-handled keypress | Pass `type` to `client.key` only through its loop. Never send your own `keyDown`. |
   101	| `editor.hasFocus()` false while focus looks right | This can't be measured over CDP. Assert the consequence instead, e.g. the cursor moved past the inserted text. |
   102	| File content assertion fails, editor looks right | Saves are debounced (about 2s). `waitFor` on `app.vault.read(...)`, and don't read once. |
   103	| `getLeaf(true)` throws "No tab group found" | Every markdown leaf was detached. Use `getLeaf("tab")`. |
   104	| Top-level `await` throws in `evaluate` | Bodies run in a plain function. Return an async IIFE or a promise chain. |
   105	| `iterateRootLeaves` count caps at 2 | A truthy callback return stops the iteration. Use a block body `{ n++; }`. |
   106	| Escape handler in a modal child never wins | Obsidian's modal scope runs first. Push a `Scope` with `app.keymap.pushScope`. |
   107	| Styling CodeMirror spans disappears on focus or scroll | Use a CM6 decoration, not MutationObserver stamping. A widget's `ignoreEvent()` must stay `true` for clicks. |
   108	| Selectors from an old ENG example don't match | The UI drifts. The node search input is now a contenteditable `[role=textbox]`, not an `<input>`. |
   109	| Flaky failure that looks like a code bug | Trang may be using the app mid-run. Rerun before believing a single observation. |
   110	| Timers stall, writes land minutes late | Focus emulation normally prevents this. If it recurs, check `document.visibilityState` and ask Trang to show the window. |
   111	| zsh eats `${VAR}` in `node -e` | Write scenarios to `.mjs` files. |
   112	| `waitFor` on an IIFE always times out | `evaluate` adds an outer `return` only when the code contains no `return`. An IIFE with an inner `return` evaluates to `undefined`, so write `return (() => { ... })()`. |
   113	| A note written in `setup` is randomly missing from search results | Datacore indexes new files after the metadata cache, and the search loads through Datacore. After `writeNote`, also `waitFor` `dc.query("@page and exists(nodeTypeId)")` to include the path. |
